mbrella' trees with wider, flatter crowns, low scrub bushes were added round the plinth, and the gravel carries scattered tufts of dry grass as in the downhill and uphill views. The plan is really polyhedral \u2014 the article's triangular matrix of three views (south, north-east, west) sets the walls at angles, not right angles \u2014 and is squared up here, since boxes can't take it; it is a candidate for SketchUp. Still guessed: the angles, the galleries' exact widths and depths, the lower unit's openings, the skylight's size and the scrub's positions."}